WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.092
Don't keep your

00:00:00.904 --> 00:00:01.965
SSH keys on

00:00:01.777 --> 00:00:02.437
disk

00:00:02.958 --> 00:00:04.762
Storing SSH keys

00:00:04.574 --> 00:00:05.670
as plain files

00:00:05.482 --> 00:00:06.413
on disk is

00:00:06.224 --> 00:00:07.132
riskier than it

00:00:06.944 --> 00:00:07.533
looks

00:00:07.734 --> 00:00:08.936
this post explains

00:00:08.748 --> 00:00:09.774
the threat and

00:00:09.621 --> 00:00:10.210
what to do

00:00:10.022 --> 00:00:10.752
instead

00:00:11.278 --> 00:00:12.068
To just make

00:00:11.879 --> 00:00:13.377
this absolutely clear

00:00:13.625 --> 00:00:14.497
this means that

00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:15.287
the private keys

00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:16.101
are vulnerable to

00:00:15.912 --> 00:00:17.115
be exiltrated by

00:00:16.927 --> 00:00:18.329
malicious code scanning

00:00:18.141 --> 00:00:18.966
my disk

00:00:19.502 --> 00:00:20.810
After reading articles

00:00:20.622 --> 00:00:21.518
like I deleted

00:00:21.365 --> 00:00:22.438
all my SSH

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:22.862
keys

00:00:22.957 --> 00:00:24.160
I finally decided

00:00:23.971 --> 00:00:24.525
to take the

00:00:24.337 --> 00:00:25.115
next step

00:00:25.139 --> 00:00:25.881
and get them

00:00:25.693 --> 00:00:26.589
off disk

00:00:27.126 --> 00:00:28.140
Full story on

00:00:27.951 --> 00:00:28.847
the dashboard
